        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "verso",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>and cleanness. I will give to you as [your] ke[tubba money]</li>\n<li>twelve and a half zuz, as is [due you]</li>\n<li>according to the Torah. And I will give [to you an addition]</li>\n<li>of \u27e6twenty-five dina[rs]\u27e7 {[t]hirty dinars},</li>\n<li>of which I have [already] advanced to you te[n dinars,]</li>\n<li>and there rem[a]in for you, incumbent upon me, twenty d[inars],</li>\n<li>delayed, as a debt. And this is the dowry which [you] brou[ght]</li>\n<li>to [me].\" (Then) he writes the enti[re] trousseau, every</li>\n<li>item with its value. Whe[n] there remains no-</li>\n<li>thing, he totals it a[l]]: And the</li>\n<li>total of this marriage contract, the mohar</li>\n<li>the additional gift, and the dowry, is so many of gold</li>\n<li>and twelve and a half zuz. \"And I,</li>\n<li>Saadiah the \u1e25azzan b. \u1e62edaqa</li>\n<li>the&nbsp;\u1e25azzan, m(ay his) s(oul be) b(ound) i(n the bundle of) l(ife), undertake the secur[it]y of this marriage</li>\n<li>contract, upon me and upon my [h]eirs after me,</li>\n<li>to be collectable by you [from] all the best (and) choice [of my possessions...\"]</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
